      "result": {
        "summary": "Fix round addresses both prior failures: cli.py now imports Path before use in the planner-context branch (fixes UnboundLocalError), and planner-prompt.sh ends with explicit exit 0 so a non-matching `[ -n \"$out\" ]` no longer propagates a nonzero exit (fixes AssertionError 1 != 0). planner_context.context_tokens/hook_message match the spec: sums input_tokens+cache_read_input_tokens+cache_creation_input_tokens from the newest transcript's last usage-bearing message, returns None when absent, and hook_message emits the one-line reminder only at/above threshold. Ran tests/test_planner_context.py and tests/test_hooks.py directly (PYTHONPATH=tests): all pass, including the new test_hook_message_over_threshold and test_prompt_hook_context_threshold, and the existing test_prompt_hook still passes unchanged.",
